  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts with a custom-shader water scene and a sky dome. It passes `typecheck`, but I couldn't run it or `vite build`, so it has never been rendered.\n\n- **Water:** a 256×256 grid whose spacing is finest near the camera, displaced by four summed sine waves in the vertex shader, so the waves are real geometry. The fragment shader recomputes the wave normals and adds a three-octave value-noise ripple that fades with distance. It then applies Schlick fresnel mixing deep water colour with the reflected sky, a tight and a broad Blinn-Phong sun glint, and distance haze to the horizon colour. A `waveClock` uniform is updated every frame.\n- **Sky:** an inward-facing sphere using the same gradient function (horizon, mid, zenith, sun glow and disc) that the water samples for its reflection.\n- **Colour output:** the shaders write linear light from sRGB-authored colours, with a soft highlight shoulder, and the app sets `output: { toneMapping: \"none\" }`. This follows the docs' colour contract, but I couldn't confirm the option takes effect. If it is ignored, the default ACES tone mapping would make the image a little darker and greyer.\n- **Camera and readiness:** the camera sits 3.2 units above the water, tilted slightly down toward the horizon. I used `.then` instead of top-level `await` so the build doesn't depend on the esbuild target. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set two animation frames after `app.ready()`.\n\n",
